  "previous_run_gist": "Hidden primary-metric values from the prior run have been redacted. Use the qualitative parameter patterns and configuration hints below.\n\nPrior for new tuning run:\n\nFocus on C6 C-state utilization. Explore configurations around 75ms for latency, min_granularity_ns, and wakeup_granularity_ns. A napi_busy_poll value around 750 appears promising.\n\nAvoid very low granularity settings (20-30ms) as they tend to increase context switches and reduce IPC. Initial exploration with C1 C-states and low granularities was not productive.\n\nEarly validation guidance: Monitor for high cstate_c6_pct, low cstate_c1_pct/cstate_c1e_pct, and high cpu_load_cores_pct. Aim for moderate instructions_per_cycle (0.65-0.70) and low context_switches_per_sec/cpu_migrations_per_sec. If these signatures degrade, it suggests a move towards a risky region.\n\nThe relationship between granularity and overhead (context switches) is a key trade-off. Higher granularity values seem to be more beneficial. Confidence in parameter transfer is moderate due to the absence of direct hidden-score signal signals in the previous run; metric signatures were the primary guide."
